import Mathlib
/-!
# Line N20 — key finite facts for the H1 push (λ-carry graph, Collatz–Wielandt, Green kernel)
Grok Bot, 2026-11-01. No `sorry`, no `native_decide`; kernel evaluation (`decide +kernel`) and `norm_num` only.
v2 (memory-light): the reachable sets are given as literal bitmasks with BFS-depth certificates, instead of being
recomputed by 40 iterations inside every proof (v1 was OOM-killed at 11 GB on the shared box).

Box |e| ≤ 15 (a-priori Green bound), offset coordinates e' = e + 15 ∈ [0,30], state index s = a'·31 + b'.
* `fw_closed`/`bw_closed`: FW (BW) is closed under successors (predecessors) and contains (0,0); hence every state
  reachable from (to) (0,0) lies in FW (BW).
* `fw_depth`/`bw_depth`: every state of FW (BW) other than (0,0) has a predecessor (successor) in the set at BFS depth
  one less; hence every element of FW (BW) is reachable from (to) (0,0).  Together: FW, BW are exactly the reachable sets.
* `reach_card`: |FW ∩ BW| = 633 (states on closed paths (0,0) → (0,0)); `reach_le14`, `reach_has14`: max |e| = 14.
* `carry_cw`: Collatz–Wielandt, A x ≥ 20 x on FW ∩ BW, so ρ(A) ≥ 20.
-/
